  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Three boxes – win the ball",
  "description": "Three boxes, about 10 × 6 metres each, sit one after the other. A defender (red) stands in each box. An attacker (blue) starts with the ball in the first box and takes on the defender there. If the attacker gets past, they carry on into the next box and face the next defender.\n\nIf the defender wins the ball, they score a point by dribbling it over the line the attacker came in through. Rotate so everyone attacks and defends. With more players, send two attackers with a short gap between them.\n\nWarm-up: pairs with one ball in the penalty area. One attacks and the other defends; whoever wins the ball becomes the attacker. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Get as close to the attacker as you can – but not so close they can go past you."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Stand side-on, bend at the hips and knees and stay light on your feet."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Wait for the right moment and put your foot in when the ball is loose."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "If you are beaten: turn straight away and chase."
    }
  ],
